(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_physics_lawsofmotion=[{id:"neet-2026-q014",pn:14,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Resultant force and acceleration",q:"The magnitude and direction of the acceleration produced in a body of mass 5 kg when two mutually perpendicular forces 8 N and 6 N act on it, are respectively:",o:["2 m s\u207B\xB2; tan\u207B\xB9(3/4) with 6 N force","2 m s\u207B\xB2; tan\u207B\xB9(4/3) with 8 N force","2 m s\u207B\xB2; tan\u207B\xB9(3/4) with 8 N force","20 m s\u207B\xB2; tan\u207B\xB9(4/3) with 8 N force"],c:2,s:`F_net = \u221A(6\xB2 + 8\xB2) = 10 N.
a = F_net/m = 10/5 = 2 m/s\xB2.
tan\u03B8 = 6/8.
\u03B8 = tan\u207B\xB9(3/4), measured from the 8 N force.`,sfig:{w:200,h:125,alt:"Forces 6 N up and 8 N right with resultant F_net at angle theta from the 8 N force",d:[["l",50,100,50,15,"a"],["l",50,100,150,100,"a"],["l",50,100,125,45,"a"],["t",20,20,"6 N"],["t",130,116,"8 N","m"],["t",130,44,"F_net","s"],["p","M72 100A22 22 0 0 0 67.7 86.9"],["t",76,95,"\u03B8","s"]]}},{id:"neet-2026r-q019",pn:19,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Banking of roads",q:"A car travels on a circular racetrack of radius 50 m, which is banked at an angle \u03B8. If the car travels at a speed 10 ms\u207B\xB9, then the wear and tear on its tyres is minimum. Taking the acceleration due to gravity to be 10 ms\u207B\xB2, the value of \u03B8 is:",o:["tan\u207B\xB9(2/5)","tan\u207B\xB9(\u221A3/2)","tan\u207B\xB9(2\u221A3)","tan\u207B\xB9(1/5)"],c:3,s:`Wear and tear is minimum when no friction is needed, so tan \u03B8 = v\xB2/(rg).
tan \u03B8 = (10 \xD7 10)/(50 \xD7 10) = 1/5.
\u03B8 = tan\u207B\xB9(1/5).`},{id:"neet-2026-q035",pn:35,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Friction",q:`A box of mass 15 kg is kept on the floor of a stationary trolley. The coefficient of static friction between the box and the trolley is 0.12. Keeping the box in stationary state over the trolley, the maximum acceleration with which the trolley can be moved horizontally in m s\u207B\xB2 is:
(g = 10 m/s\xB2)`,o:["1.5","1.8","2.1","1.2"],c:3,s:`The box moves with the trolley only if the friction force can supply the needed force.
Maximum friction \u03BCmg is balanced by ma.
So a = \u03BCg = 0.12 \xD7 10 = 1.2 m/s\xB2.`,sfig:{w:150,h:90,alt:"A box on top of a trolley; an arrow labelled \u03BCmg points left and an arrow labelled ma points right at the box",d:[["r",17,27,101,46],["r",53,8,27,19],["l",53,17,38,17,"a"],["l",80,17,95,17,"a"],["t",4,21,"\u03BCmg","s"],["t",98,21,"ma","s"]]}},{id:"neet-2025-q004",pn:4,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Friction on an inclined plane",q:"There are two inclined surfaces of equal length (L) and same angle of inclination 45\xB0 with the horizontal. One of them is rough and the other is perfectly smooth. A given body takes 2 times as much time to slide down on rough surface than on the smooth surface. The coefficient of kinetic friction (\u03BC_k) between the object and the rough surface is close to",o:["0.25","0.40","0.5","0.75"],c:3,s:`t_rough = 2 t_smooth
a_smooth = g sin\u03B8
t \u221D 1/\u221Aa, so t_smooth \u221D 1/\u221A(g sin\u03B8)
a_rough = g sin\u03B8 \u2212 \u03BC_k g cos\u03B8
t_rough/t_smooth = \u221A(sin\u03B8) / \u221A(sin\u03B8 \u2212 \u03BC_k cos\u03B8) = 2
Squaring both sides: sin\u03B8/(sin\u03B8 \u2212 \u03BC_k cos\u03B8) = 4
\u21D2 (1/\u221A2) / (1/\u221A2 \u2212 \u03BC_k \xD7 1/\u221A2) = 4
\u21D2 1 \u2212 \u03BC_k = 1/4
\u03BC_k = 3/4 = 0.75`},{id:"neet-2025-q010",pn:10,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Impulse and momentum",q:"A ball of mass 0.5 kg is dropped from a height of 40 m. The ball hits the ground and rises to a height of 10 m. The impulse imparted to the ball during its collision with the ground is (Take g = 9.8 m/s\xB2)",o:["21 NS","7 NS","0","84 NS"],c:0,s:`Speed just before hitting: v\u2081 = \u221A(2gh\u2081) = \u221A(2 \xD7 9.8 \xD7 40) = \u221A784 = 28 m s\u207B\xB9
Speed just after: v\u2082 = \u221A(2gh\u2082) = \u221A(2 \xD7 9.8 \xD7 10) = \u221A196 = 14 m s\u207B\xB9
Impulse = \u0394p\u20D7 = m(v\u20D7_f \u2212 v\u20D7_i) = m(v\u20D7\u2082 \u2212 v\u20D7\u2081)
= (1/2)(14 \u2212 (\u221228))
= 21 NS`,sfig:{w:380,h:190,alt:"A ball dropped 40 m (dotted line) reaches the ground with velocity v1 downward, then rises with velocity v2 upward to 10 m; the ground is hatched.",d:[["l",96.3,7.2,96.3,155.7,"b"],["t",48.6,76.5,"40 m",""],["c",160.2,9,2.7,"F"],["l",160.2,9,160.2,153,"d"],["l",160.2,117,160.2,155.7,"a"],["t",135,137.7,"v\u2081",""],["c",186.3,67.5,2.7,"F"],["l",186.3,67.5,186.3,153,"d"],["l",186.3,154.8,186.3,114.3,"a"],["t",201.6,128.7,"v\u2082",""],["l",252.9,155.7,252.9,65.7,"b"],["t",262.8,114.3,"10 m",""],["l",110.7,157.5,324,157.5,""],["l",110.7,163.8,117,157.5,""],["l",117.9,163.8,124.2,157.5,""],["l",125.1,163.8,131.4,157.5,""],["l",132.3,163.8,138.6,157.5,""],["l",139.5,163.8,145.8,157.5,""],["l",146.7,163.8,153,157.5,""],["l",153.9,163.8,160.2,157.5,""],["l",161.1,163.8,167.4,157.5,""],["l",168.3,163.8,174.6,157.5,""],["l",175.5,163.8,181.8,157.5,""],["l",182.7,163.8,189,157.5,""],["l",189.9,163.8,196.2,157.5,""],["l",197.1,163.8,203.4,157.5,""],["l",204.3,163.8,210.6,157.5,""],["l",211.5,163.8,217.8,157.5,""],["l",218.7,163.8,225,157.5,""],["l",225.9,163.8,232.2,157.5,""],["l",233.1,163.8,239.4,157.5,""],["l",240.3,163.8,246.6,157.5,""],["l",247.5,163.8,253.8,157.5,""],["l",254.7,163.8,261,157.5,""],["l",261.9,163.8,268.2,157.5,""],["l",269.1,163.8,275.4,157.5,""],["l",276.3,163.8,282.6,157.5,""],["l",283.5,163.8,289.8,157.5,""],["l",290.7,163.8,297,157.5,""],["l",297.9,163.8,304.2,157.5,""],["l",305.1,163.8,311.4,157.5,""],["l",312.3,163.8,318.6,157.5,""],["l",319.5,163.8,325.8,157.5,""]]}},{id:"neet-2024-q009",pn:9,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Contact force between two blocks",q:"A horizontal force 10 N is applied to a block A as shown in figure. The mass of blocks A and B are 2 kg and 3 kg, respectively. The blocks slide over a frictionless surface. The force exerted by block A on block B is-",o:["6 N","10 N","zero","4 N"],c:0,s:`Treat A and B as one system: F = (M\u2081 + M\u2082)a.
a = 10/(2 + 3) = 2 m s\u207B\xB2.
Force of A on B, F\u2032 = M\u2082a = 3 \xD7 2 = 6 N.`,fig:{w:250,h:95,alt:"A horizontal force F = 10 N pushes block A (2 kg), which touches block B (3 kg), on a frictionless horizontal surface.",d:[["t",10,52,"F = 10 N"],["l",10,66,128,66,"a"],["r",130,50,42,30],["r",172,28,42,52],["t",151,61,"A","m"],["t",151,74,"2 kg","ms"],["t",193,46,"B","m"],["t",193,60,"3 kg","m"],["l",100,80,230,80],["l",104,80,99,86],["l",110,80,105,86],["l",116,80,111,86],["l",122,80,117,86],["l",128,80,123,86],["l",134,80,129,86],["l",140,80,135,86],["l",146,80,141,86],["l",152,80,147,86],["l",158,80,153,86],["l",164,80,159,86],["l",170,80,165,86],["l",176,80,171,86],["l",182,80,177,86],["l",188,80,183,86],["l",194,80,189,86],["l",200,80,195,86],["l",206,80,201,86],["l",212,80,207,86],["l",218,80,213,86],["l",224,80,219,86],["l",230,80,225,86]]}},{id:"neet-2024-q034",pn:34,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Circular motion tension",q:"A bob is whirled in a horizontal plane by means of a string with an initial speed of \u03C9 rpm. The tension in the string is T. If speed becomes 2\u03C9 while keeping the same radius, the tension in the string becomes;",o:["T/4","\u221A2 T","T","4T"],c:3,s:`Tension gives the centripetal force: T = m\u2113\u03C9\xB2.
With 2\u03C9: T\u2032 = m\u2113(2\u03C9)\xB2 = 4m\u2113\u03C9\xB2.
So T\u2032 = 4T.`,sfig:{w:140,h:150,alt:"Two sketches of a bob of mass m on a string of length l rotating about a fixed point, with angular speed omega and then 2 omega, tension T pointing towards the centre.",d:[["c",16,40,2,"F"],["l",16,40,102,40],["c",106,40,4],["l",100,40,84,40,"a"],["t",86,32,"T"],["t",108,32,"m"],["t",54,58,"\u2113"],["p","M26 64 Q44 40 26 22","a"],["t",8,18,"\u03C9"],["c",16,120,2,"F"],["l",16,120,102,120],["c",106,120,4],["l",100,120,84,120,"a"],["t",86,112,"T"],["t",108,112,"m"],["t",54,138,"\u2113"],["p","M26 144 Q44 120 26 102","a"],["t",8,98,"2\u03C9"]]}},{id:"neet-2023-q004",pn:4,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Force and change of momentum",q:"A football player is moving southward and suddenly turns eastward with the same speed to avoid an opponent. The force that acts on the player while turning is :",o:["along south-west","along eastward","along northward","along north-east"],c:3,s:`Take east as \xEE and north as \u0135.
Final momentum Pf = mu \xEE. Initial momentum Pi = mu(\u2212\u0135).
Change in momentum \u0394P = Pf \u2212 Pi = mu \xEE + mu \u0135 = mu(\xEE + \u0135).
Force F = \u0394P/\u0394t has the same direction as the change in momentum.
So the force acts along north-east.`,sfig:{w:200,h:170,alt:"Compass axes: \u0135 north (up), \xEE east (right), west left, south down.",d:[["l",100,85,100,18,"a"],["l",100,85,100,152,"a"],["l",100,85,22,85,"a"],["l",100,85,178,85,"a"],["t",90,22,"\u0135","e"],["t",106,22,"N"],["t",186,89,"E"],["t",8,89,"W"],["t",184,78,"\xEE"],["t",106,164,"S"]]}},{id:"neet-2023-q046",pn:46,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Friction and pseudo force",q:"Calculate the maximum acceleration of a moving car so that a body lying on the floor of the car remains stationary, The coefficient of static friction between the body and the floor is 0.15 (g = 10 ms\u207B\xB2)",o:["50 ms\u207B\xB2","1.2 ms\u207B\xB2","150 ms\u207B\xB2","1.5 ms\u207B\xB2"],c:3,s:`In the car's frame the body is at rest, so the pseudo force m\xB7a_max is balanced by limiting friction.
m\xB7a_max = \u03BC_s\xB7m\xB7g.
a_max = \u03BC_s g = 0.15 \xD7 10 = 1.5 m/s\xB2.`,sfig:{w:280,h:190,alt:"Block on the floor of a car that accelerates to the right with a_max; free-body diagram of the block: m\xB7a_max to the left and friction f_r to the right.",d:[["l",10,60,200,60],["r",35,30,90,24],["t",80,46,"car","m"],["r",70,20,12,10],["t",90,18,"block"],["c",55,66,6,""],["c",95,66,6,""],["l",135,40,185,40,"a"],["r",70,115,70,60],["l",140,145,200,145,"a"],["t",191,44,"a"],["t",198,47,"max","s"],["l",112,145,78,145,"a"],["l",140,145,200,145,"a"],["t",206,141,"f"],["t",211,144,"r","s"],["t",20,141,"ma"],["t",36,144,"max","s"]]}},{id:"neet-2022r-q007",pn:7,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Linear momentum",q:"The distance covered by a body of mass 5 g having linear momentum 0.3 kg m/s in 5 s is:",o:["0.3 m","300 m","30 m","3 m"],c:1,s:`Momentum p = mv, with m = 5 g = 5/1000 kg.
0.3 = (5/1000) \xD7 v, so v = 60 m/s.
Distance in 5 s = 60 \xD7 5 = 300 m.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q031",pn:31,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Contact force on incline",q:"In the diagram shown, the normal reaction force between 2 kg and 1 kg is (Consider the surface, to be smooth): Given g = 10 ms\u207B\xB2",o:["10 N","25 N","39 N","6 N"],c:1,s:`Take all three blocks together. Net force up the incline = 60 \u2212 18 \u2212 (3+2+1)g sin30\xB0 = 60 \u2212 18 \u2212 30 = 12 N.
Acceleration a = 12/6 = 2 m/s\xB2 up the incline.
For the 1 kg block: N \u2212 18 \u2212 1\xD710\xD7sin30\xB0 = 1\xD72.
N \u2212 23 = 2, so N = 25 N.`,fig:{w:350,h:200,alt:"A smooth incline of angle 30 degrees with blocks of 3 kg, 2 kg and 1 kg in contact; a 60 N force F1 pushes the 3 kg block up the slope and an 18 N force F2 pushes the 1 kg block down the slope.",d:[["l",20,185,330,185],["l",64,185,280.5063509461097,60,""],["p","M133.3 145L183.5 116L171.5 95.2L121.3 124.2Z"],["p","M183.5 116L223.3 93L211.3 72.2L171.5 95.2Z"],["p","M223.3 93L256.3 74L244.3 53.2L211.3 72.2Z"],["t",132.89676901250382,103.65321248268239,"3 kg","s"],["t",177.93009000929464,77.65321248268239,"2 kg","s"],["t",214.30315696824107,56.6532124826824,"1 kg","s"],["l",92.64101615137756,154.60769515458674,127.28203230275511,134.60769515458674,"a"],["t",30.641016151377556,157.60769515458674,"F\u2081 = 60 N","s"],["l",284.89865579152297,43.607695154586736,250.25763964014538,63.607695154586736,"a"],["t",292.89865579152297,39.607695154586736,"F\u2082 = 18 N","s"],["p","M98 185A34 34 0 0 0 93.4 168"],["t",106,181,"\u03B8 = 30\xB0","s"]]}},{id:"neet-2021-q046",pn:46,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Laws of Motion",st:"Impulse",q:"A ball of mass 0.15 kg is dropped from a height 10 m, strikes the ground and rebounds to the same height. The magnitude of impulse imparted to the ball is (g = 10 m/s\xB2) nearly",o:["1.4 kg m/s","0 kg m/s","4.2 kg m/s","2.1 kg m/s"],c:2,s:`Speed just before and just after hitting the ground: v = \u221A(2gh) = \u221A(2 \xD7 10 \xD7 10) = 10\u221A2 \u2248 14.1 m/s (it rebounds to the same height).
The direction reverses, so change in momentum = m(v \u2013 (\u2013v)) = 2mv.
Impulse = 2 \xD7 0.15 \xD7 14.1 \u2248 4.2 kg m/s.`}]})();
